<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Agent-to-agent communication · Agentic Bible</title><meta name="description" content="How agents exchange messages, task state and artifacts across an interface, with separate checks for interoperability, authority and result quality."><meta property="og:title" content="Agent-to-agent communication · Agentic Bible"><meta property="og:description" content="How agents exchange messages, task state and artifacts across an interface, with separate checks for interoperability, authority and result quality."><meta property="og:type" content="article"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Agentic Bible"><meta property="og:url" content="https://agenticbible.si/articles/agent-to-agent-communication/"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary"><meta name="twitter:title" content="Agent-to-agent communication · Agentic Bible"><meta name="twitter:description" content="How agents exchange messages, task state and artifacts across an interface, with separate checks for interoperability, authority and result quality."><meta name="robots" content="index, follow"><meta name="color-scheme" content="light"><link rel="canonical" href="https://agenticbible.si/articles/agent-to-agent-communication/"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"TechArticle","headline":"Agent-to-agent communication","description":"How agents exchange messages, task state and artifacts across an interface, with separate checks for interoperability, authority and result quality.","articleSection":"Protocols","inLanguage":"en","url":"https://agenticbible.si/articles/agent-to-agent-communication/","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://agenticbible.si/articles/agent-to-agent-communication/"},"citation":["https://a2a-protocol.org/v0.3.0/specification/","https://www.jsonrpc.org/specification","https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/architecture"]}</script><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/Base.DyzAbnuc.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/_id_.w1YKO1jA.css"></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header shell"><a class="wordmark" href="/"><img src="/favicon.svg" width="36" height="36" alt=""><span>Agentic Bible<span class="wordmark-sub">A living reference</span></span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/" aria-current="page">Library</a><a href="/topics/">Topics</a><a href="/about/">About</a><a href="/history/">History</a></nav><a class="header-search" href="/search/" aria-label="Search the library"><svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></circle><path d="m13 13 4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></path></svg><span>Search</span><kbd aria-hidden="true">/</kbd></a></header><div class="preview-strip" role="region" aria-label="Edition status"><div class="shell"><span class="status-dot"></span> Preview edition <span class="strip-detail">Sourced working drafts. Editorial review pending.</span></div></div><main id="main" class="shell" tabindex="-1"><div class="article-breadcrumb" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Library</a><span data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>/</span><a href="/topics/protocols/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Protocols</a></div><div class="reading-layout" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><article class="article" data-pagefind-body data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><header id="overview" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p class="eyebrow" data-pagefind-meta="topic" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Protocols / Reference entry 18</p><h1 data-pagefind-meta="title" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Agent-to-agent communication</h1><p class="article-deck" data-pagefind-meta="description" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>How agents exchange messages, task state and artifacts across an interface, with separate checks for interoperability, authority and result quality.</p><div class="article-status" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span class="draft-pill" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span class="status-dot" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></span> Working draft</span><span data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Human editorial certification pending</span></div><nav class="article-actions" aria-label="Article actions" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="#sources" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Sources (3)</a><a href="#revision" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision history</a><a href="#share" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Share or cite</a><a href="/contribute/?article=agent-to-agent-communication" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Contribution options</a></nav></header><aside class="contents" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><details data-article-contents data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><summary data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>On this page</summary><nav aria-label="On this page" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="#overview" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Overview</a><a href="#separate-a-message-from-completed-work" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Separate a message from completed work</a><a href="#correlation-is-not-a-delivery-guarantee" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Correlation is not a delivery guarantee</a><a href="#interfaces-have-different-scopes" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Interfaces have different scopes</a><a href="#evaluate-the-whole-exchange" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Evaluate the whole exchange</a><a href="#sources" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Sources & context</a><a href="#revision" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision record</a></nav></details><div class="contents-bottom" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><span class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Part of the collection</span><a href="/topics/protocols/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Protocols <svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></a></div></aside><div class="prose" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p><strong>Agent-to-agent communication</strong> is the exchange of requests, observations or work products between agent systems. It needs an interface that the participants interpret consistently. A2A version 0.3.0 provides one such contract: an Agent Card advertises identity, capabilities, skills and connection information; messages, tasks and artifacts represent interaction and outputs. The card describes a service’s claims and interface, rather than certifying that it can perform every advertised task correctly. <a href="#source-a2a">1</a></p>
<h2 id="separate-a-message-from-completed-work">Separate a message from completed work</h2>
<p>In an original reference-library example, one agent asks another to compare two specification revisions. A message can acknowledge receipt before the comparison is finished. A later artifact might contain the proposed differences and evidence references. A useful interface would preserve which event means “received,” which means “needs input” and which means “finished.” Treating every response as final would collapse those distinct states.</p>
<p>The pinned A2A specification describes task states including working, input-required and terminal outcomes, and distinguishes messages from artifacts. Those types help participants represent progress under that contract. They do not establish the factual correctness of an artifact or grant access to a protected source. Both sides still need compatible versions, supported interaction modes and an authorization arrangement. <a href="#source-a2a">1</a></p>
<h2 id="correlation-is-not-a-delivery-guarantee">Correlation is not a delivery guarantee</h2>
<p>JSON-RPC 2.0 defines request and response objects with matching identifiers, while a notification omits an identifier and receives no response. It is transport agnostic. Those rules help match a reply to a call; they do not establish that a business task completed, nor do they supply exactly-once execution for an external effect. <a href="#source-jsonrpc">2</a></p>
<p>A2A supports multiple protocol bindings, so one should inspect the selected binding rather than assume all exchanges use JSON-RPC. <a href="#source-a2a">1</a></p>
<p>Suppose the comparison service becomes unreachable after receiving a request. The caller could know that it sent bytes while remaining uncertain whether work began. Retrying requires an agreed identity for the work and a policy for duplicate handling. <a href="/articles/durable-agent-execution/">Durable execution</a> examines that broader problem. A network acknowledgment and a completed comparison are different evidence even if they arrive on the same connection.</p>
<h2 id="interfaces-have-different-scopes">Interfaces have different scopes</h2>
<p>The cited MCP architecture defines host, client and server components for connecting an AI application with capabilities and context. It offers a different interface example from A2A’s task exchange. An application can combine protocols or wrap one behind another, so their names alone do not establish a universal boundary between “tools” and “agents.” Inspect actual messages, version support and responsibilities. <a href="#source-mcp-architecture">3</a></p>
<p><a href="/articles/agent-orchestration/">Orchestration</a> concerns how the overall work is coordinated. Communication concerns what crosses a particular interface. A coordinator could exchange messages with several services without sharing its complete internal state. Conversely, a multi-component system might coordinate everything within one process and have no external agent protocol at all. This entry focuses on the exchange boundary rather than prescribing a multi-agent topology.</p>
<h2 id="evaluate-the-whole-exchange">Evaluate the whole exchange</h2>
<p>For the original example, useful tests would include an unsupported skill, a request needing clarification, duplicate submission and a validly formatted artifact with an unsupported claim. The receiving agent should distinguish these cases instead of treating every problem as a transport failure. <a href="/articles/structured-outputs/">Structured outputs</a> covers form; <a href="/articles/agent-evaluation/">evaluation</a> covers outcomes and evidence.</p>
<p>A participant’s message also remains untrusted input with respect to the receiver’s authority. An instruction to fetch a private document should pass the applicable <a href="/articles/agent-identity/">identity and delegation</a> and permission checks. Communication is useful when it makes task state and responsibility explicit. It cannot supply missing authority, consistent semantics or reliable results merely by adding another agent.</p>
</div><p class="article-feedback" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="/contribute/?article=agent-to-agent-communication" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Suggest a correction or primary source</a> · Public intake remains on hold; the local synthetic form covers only the original three entries.</p><section class="sources" id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-title" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Follow the evidence</p><h2 id="sources-title" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Sources & context</h2><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Primary sources checked on <time datetime="2026-10-17" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>17 October 2026</time>. A source check is not independent editorial approval.</p><ol data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><li id="source-a2a" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="https://a2a-protocol.org/v0.3.0/specification/" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Agent2Agent Protocol specification, v0.3.0 <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></span></a><span class="source-publisher" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>A2A Protocol</span><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Version 0.3.0; Agent Cards, messages, tasks, artifacts and lifecycle. This pinned version is not a claim about the newest specification.</p></li><li id="source-jsonrpc" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="https://www.jsonrpc.org/specification" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>JSON-RPC 2.0 Specification <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></span></a><span class="source-publisher" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>JSON-RPC Working Group</span><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Origin 26 March 2010, updated 4 January 2013; sections 1, 4–6. Request identifiers correlate responses; notifications have no response.</p></li><li id="source-mcp-architecture" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/architecture" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>MCP architecture, 2025-11-25 <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></span></a><span class="source-publisher" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Model Context Protocol</span><p data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Version 2025-11-25; host/client/server architecture and connections. Used as a separate interface example, not a universal division of protocol roles.</p></li></ol></section><section class="revision" id="revision" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><h2 data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision record</h2><dl data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Authorship</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>AI-assisted project draft</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Source check</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><time datetime="2026-10-17" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>17 October 2026</time>. This records source consultation, not editorial certification.</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Human editorial review</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Pending. No human editorial certification is recorded.</dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Latest source change</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><time datetime="2026-10-17" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>17 October 2026</time> · Complete twenty sourced working drafts with bounded catalog validation · <code data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>d3c80414</code></dd></div><div data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><dt data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Revision receipt</dt><dd data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>No separate publication receipt is recorded for this working draft.</dd></div></dl><p class="review-scope" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>The twenty entries received deep reading across external and internal review. Claim verification was sampled; this does not certify every factual claim.</p><a class="text-link" data-source-commit="8a38252384c6fe6024a75b462ad95294a131100c" href="https://github.com/Leshey-Digital/agentic-bible/commits/8a38252384c6fe6024a75b462ad95294a131100c/src/content/articles/agent-to-agent-communication.md" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>View file history on GitHub <svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2></path></svg></a></section><section class="share-tools" id="share" aria-labelledby="share-title" data-pagefind-ignore data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><p class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Keep a useful reference</p><h2 id="share-title" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Share or cite this entry</h2><p id="article-citation" tabindex="0" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>“Agent-to-agent communication.” Agentic Bible. https://agenticbible.si/articles/agent-to-agent-communication/</p><div class="share-buttons" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2><button type="button" data-copy-link hidden data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Copy article link</button><button type="button" data-copy-citation hidden data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>Copy citation</button></div><p class="share-status" data-share-status role="status" aria-live="polite" data-astro-cid-poxfbvb2>The citation and link above remain available to copy manually if clipboard access is unavailable.</p></section><section class="